WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:02.268
- Tonight is a very special night.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.904
There's a little event coming up called the All-Star game.

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.873
Now there is something that has been missing.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.775
The All-Star draft.

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:10.710
We are bringing it back from the dead.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.146
And today we have a very special guest.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:15.048
It is Biz Nasty.

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:16.082
Biz, Where ya at?

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.017
What're you up to here, buddy?

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.518
- Don't worry about where I am, buddy.

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:22.589
You seem a little bit nervous off that intro.
You OK? What's your heart rate at?

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:23.156
About 180 beats per minute?

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:23.456
- That was smooth!

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.592
No stumbling over the words. I'm dressed nice.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.861
You just showed up with a cowboy hat on, all right.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:30.163
- I'm going Bill Belichick style here,

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:30.530
OK?

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.366
I'm also, I'm gonna be all serious, but very laid back.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.535
Like he was at the draft with the, with the

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.771
dog at the house at the, at the dinner table.

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:38.905
- OK,

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:39.606
I like that.

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:41.207
So let me run you through the rules real quick.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.143
We're gonna do a 10-player draft with

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:45.345
all of the choices of the players available.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.080
You can sort that however you want.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.783
If you don't wanna have any defenders on your team, you don't need them.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:50.550
Sound good?

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:51.818
- That sounds great,

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:54.354
I like those rules. Now, how are we gonna decide who goes first?

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:56.956
- Uh, I have a deck of cards.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:58.892
Do you have a deck of cards, as well?

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:00.560
- I have a deck of cards.

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:02.162
- You do have a deck of cards.
- And I have,

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:04.731
and I have a stopwatch because there's a time limit on this.

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:08.868
I'm gonna put your mind in a pretzel all night long on the draft board here.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.070
So let's— what are we doing?

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.572
Drawing highest card for who gets the first pick?

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:16.609
- Let's see a legit, I want to see an actual bridge shuffle going down.

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:16.976
OK.

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:17.310
Yes.

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:17.911
I like this.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:18.611
I will do the same.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:21.781
- Here, I'll even close my laptop and close my eyes for you,

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:22.282
OK?

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:24.517
Cuz you probably think I'm cheating.
- Highest card wins here, all right?

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:29.022
Three, two, one. I got a two.

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:32.659
- Oh! Good start for Bizzy Boy!

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.061
- I think we're ready to go.
- OK.

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:36.129
- You wanna get us started here?

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.198
I'll, uh, I'll put 30 seconds on the clock.

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:39.599
I don't know if you're gonna take that long here

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.501
for Pick One, but we'll see what you have in store.

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:43.736
- We already have a jersey made for this guy.

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:47.140
We got Andrei Vasilevskiy, OK?

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:50.276
The foundation to any great team is in goal.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:54.114
And you look at the last two playoff runs they had, back-to-back championships,

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:58.585
he didn't lose back-to-back games one time on the way to two Stanley cups.

00:01:58.585 --> 00:02:02.555
So he's a bread winner, and he's gonna be the foundation to our team.

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:05.425
Welcome to the squad, Vasilevskiy.

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:08.528
I'm just gonna stick with his last name here and keep it really simple.

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:09.929
I think everybody gets the point.

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.399
Maybe shorten it, put just Vasy on there.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:15.268
Just so you get the spelling correct.

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:17.837
And another thing too, a little fun fact for you,

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:20.507
people at home, I was not maybe the biggest cat person.

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:24.010
And then I got to sit down with Vasilevskiy at, uh, the NHL

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:27.213
media scrums in Chicago one year before the season started.

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:30.283
And he actually got me to, uh, to start liking cats.

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:34.053
So the guy has a tons of power and tons of influence, and he's gonna

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:36.623
have a ton of influence in that locker room on winning some games.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:38.625
- I liked that Biz.

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:39.159
I like that.

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:43.229
All right, my first pick, you know, this is a tough one, right?

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:46.933
Uh, I, I think my goal for this draft is just

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.735
to not get chirped too hard on the internet.

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:52.071
So you took Vasy No. 1, which is maybe a bit questionable.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:54.440
I think you, you will maybe get some hate for that.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:57.243
I'm gonna go ahead and take the man, the guy that's gonna

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.345
go through four guys on the ice when there's only three

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:03.449
out there, Connor McDavid at, uh, at my first overall pick.

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:07.253
- [Snoring sound] With all the drama they got going on right now.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:10.056
I don't want those types of headaches in my locker room to be quite frank.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:15.295
I don't want their, their media following my team, getting, giving harassing

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:18.665
questions in the media scrums, if by chance they lose a three-on-three match.

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:23.269
So, I mean, I'd say easily a rookie mistake in your first All-Star selection.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.103
There, Nasher, but uh.

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:24.904
- Go ahead and take it away.

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:25.605
Pick No. 2.

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:29.375
- Well, I'm gonna have to go with my former, well, I guess

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:32.478
current, still current, he did chirp me about being cheap cuz

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:34.747
I walked out on the bill one time, but that's nor here nor there.

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.317
Local Arizona kid.

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:39.385
He's going to his fourth All-Star Game.

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:42.188
He's got 10 goals in his last eight road games.

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:43.856
So he can't just get it done at home.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:45.024
He gets it done on the road.

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:49.629
Uh, his sixth season as a Maple Leaf, 25 tucks each of those seasons

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:55.168
Auston Matthews, and a little dedication to Auston with a stash. Pablo!

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.003
Welcome to the lineup.

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:58.304
Woo-wee!

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:01.774
- I like that pick, Biz, I like that pick. Ah, I thought

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:04.711
about taking him No. 1, it was definitely a toss up.

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:05.645
That's a good one though.

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:06.713
You can't go wrong with that.

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:09.115
- And he's also getting the C on my squad,

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:10.016
OK?

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:13.453
I'm taking a right off of my, uh, my chest here and I'm giving it to him.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.756
All right, you left the combo alive. Draisaitl,

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:18.458
he's gonna be playing with some angry.

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:21.661
He's gonna be playing with some fire after the interview that went down today.

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:24.130
Uh, we're going to be taking Draisaitl, putting

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.632
him and McDavid on line No. 1 here.

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.233
Is it my turn now?

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:29.702
You got your, your guy written down? Huberdeau.

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:30.370
- I do have him written down.

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:33.773
We went from the most, uh, Barkov being the most underrated player in

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:36.676
the league to Huberdeau. He's leading the league in assists by three.

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:40.179
I think he's got 38 on the year and who's gonna feed the

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:43.149
puck to one of the nastiest goal-scorers on the planet, Matthews?

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:44.550
The best passer.

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:46.519
So huge rookie mistake by you

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:49.789
Huby, and we're on nickname basis by the way, Huby.

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:51.457
- Yeah, I figured you would be.

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:53.526
I figured it would be, that's a tough one to spell as well.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:56.062
- And he's got the assistant captaincy, as well.

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:59.098
His, uh, his agent Allan Walsh will probably be giving it to you

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:01.834
on Twitter for not picking him too and giving them the snub there.

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:03.369
- Listen, we're not going to be intimidated by

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:05.338
any agents here, Biz. We're all business,

00:05:05.505 --> 00:05:05.872
all right?

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:08.274
So you gotta, you got Huby in there.

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:13.546
Uh, now the thing is, do I, do I want to focus on the D this early on?

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:18.217
There, I think there's a clear No. 1 defenseman in this draft and I, you

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:22.255
know what? He may as well be a Forward, we're taking the elite edge machine.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:24.957
The guy that only scores nasty goals.

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:28.328
Cale Makar, toss 'em in that first-line D.

00:05:29.262 --> 00:05:33.333
- I mean, I can't, I can't deny that pick. He's, uh, to me he's probably

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:36.135
the most impressive defenseman since Paul Coffey came around.

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:38.338
Now, I wasn't really around for much of Paul Coffey's

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:41.007
career cuz I was so young and, and wasn't really able

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:43.876
to absorb it and give it the credit that it deserves.

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:46.446
But Rick Tocchet told me a lot of similarities

00:05:46.446 --> 00:05:47.914
in the way he moves up and down the ice.

00:05:47.914 --> 00:05:50.016
So I can't fault you for that one.

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:54.921
Speaking of snubs, this next guy, I, the fact that he wasn't, uh, or

00:05:54.921 --> 00:05:58.991
it had to go to the last man standing and for him to get voted in, uh,

00:05:59.025 --> 00:06:01.928
he's gonna be coming into this All-Star Game, extremely motivated.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:03.696
Uh let's hope he keeps it on the rails,

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:04.731
unlike Playoffs.

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:08.468
Uh, this is actually going to be his first All-Star Game, shockingly.

00:06:08.468 --> 00:06:10.269
He's fifth in league scoring right now.

00:06:10.403 --> 00:06:12.739
That's why I'm shocked that he was snubbed to begin with.

00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:16.476
And, and, not to boot, it's a contract year and we

00:06:16.476 --> 00:06:19.011
all know how much the moolah motivates guys.
- Yup

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:23.216
Welcome to the squad, Nazem Kadri! Woo-wee!

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:24.083
- I love it, dude.

00:06:24.851 --> 00:06:26.953
There was nothing more hype than when he buried that

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:29.322
shootout winner with the announcer yelling about him

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:31.724
heading to Vegas, and then him actually getting voted in.

00:06:31.724 --> 00:06:33.693
You just, you can't write a better story than that one.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.328
- I'll give him an "A" too.

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:36.763
No, it was great.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:39.332
And, uh, he plays with an edge too.

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:41.768
So keep your, tell your guys to keep their heads up out there.

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:45.271
- All right, Biz. I, uh, I'm at a loss of words as to

00:06:45.271 --> 00:06:47.874
how this player is still available in the draft.

00:06:48.274 --> 00:06:50.243
Probably the funniest guy in the league.

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:52.145
Uh, last time when there was an NHL All-Star

00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:54.981
draft, this guy was begging to be picked last.

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:57.150
He's not getting picked last today.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:07:00.887
We are taking Alexander Ovechkin, sitting him in that left circle

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:04.590
and, uh, guaranteeing at least a hat trick game out of him.

00:07:04.791 --> 00:07:05.925
- He's an electric factory.

00:07:05.925 --> 00:07:09.262
I don't blame that pick going back to a few All-Star Games ago. And a little

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:11.864
fun fact for you people at home, I believe he's going to be leading the

00:07:11.864 --> 00:07:15.268
way with his eighth nod for everybody involved in this All-Star Game.

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:18.404
Twenty guys, it's their first time. But I forget which one it was.

00:07:18.404 --> 00:07:20.773
It might've been the All-Star Game in Montreal at the Bell

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:23.976
Centre where he put the cowboy hat on and he electrified the crowd.
- [Laughing]

00:07:23.976 --> 00:07:26.879
- So this guy, I don't blame you for that pick.

00:07:27.246 --> 00:07:29.515
So I wish I could smack-talk you, but I can't.

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:32.819
This pick for me might come out a little bit off the board, but

00:07:32.819 --> 00:07:36.489
in this type of format, you need also forwards being responsible

00:07:36.489 --> 00:07:39.125
cuz there aren't many defensemen. And I can't think of a better

00:07:39.192 --> 00:07:42.762
200-foot forward in the National Hockey League than Mark Stone.

00:07:43.129 --> 00:07:43.463
OK.

00:07:43.563 --> 00:07:44.597
Always up for the Selke.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.232
He can contribute on offense.

00:07:46.332 --> 00:07:47.867
He's gonna be great in the locker room.

00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:50.036
He's used to that chaotic environment.

00:07:50.303 --> 00:07:54.474
If I said that properly—chaotic—and it's at home for him.

00:07:54.807 --> 00:07:59.178
- Is this his first All-Star as well?
- Mine? No, I usually -

00:07:59.178 --> 00:08:01.481
- No, Mark's. No, Stoner. Oh, yeah, you.

00:08:02.014 --> 00:08:04.450
- I just thought you were bringing up the fact that I was a two-time

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:08.921
ECHL All-Star in the minors, so I just must have crossed my mind there.

00:08:08.921 --> 00:08:10.690
- We will move on.

00:08:11.357 --> 00:08:13.826
Again, I mean, we're talking electric guys, I think

00:08:14.026 --> 00:08:16.896
with this All-Star Game, I mean, you got Stoner there.

00:08:16.896 --> 00:08:19.499
It's nice to get the guys that are in there first, right?

00:08:19.499 --> 00:08:21.501
There's a little bit of hype, a little bit of buzz.

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:23.769
Ah, we're gonna take Kirill the Thrill.

00:08:23.769 --> 00:08:26.005
Kaprizov. This guy has been flying out there.

00:08:26.005 --> 00:08:28.274
Young guy, first time in an All-Star Game.

00:08:28.641 --> 00:08:31.978
No shot he goes out there and does not put on a show for us.

00:08:32.845 --> 00:08:35.114
- I mean, I just, I like the pick because Ovi's

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:37.049
gonna make him comfortable in the locker room, right?

00:08:37.049 --> 00:08:38.551
You have that Russian connection.
- Yup.

00:08:38.751 --> 00:08:40.720
- And as far as Kaprizov's concerned

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:42.822
he's used to the big stage as well.

00:08:42.822 --> 00:08:44.524
He scored the sh— what was it?

00:08:44.524 --> 00:08:48.961
The overtime winner in the gold-medal game against Germany in the last Olympics.

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:51.597
So they're probably gonna be trying to take it out on my squad,

00:08:51.597 --> 00:08:54.066
given the fact that they can't go represent their countries this year.

00:08:54.066 --> 00:08:55.735
So, I mean,
- That's a good point.

00:08:55.735 --> 00:08:58.137
- All-Star Game, Olympics, I mean, competitive nature.

00:08:58.137 --> 00:08:59.305
It's neck and neck.

00:08:59.405 --> 00:08:59.605
- Yup.

00:09:00.139 --> 00:09:00.806
I love it, man.

00:09:01.173 --> 00:09:03.276
Hey, you're hyping up, you're hyping up my

00:09:03.276 --> 00:09:05.511
picks for me, which I do greatly appreciate here.

00:09:05.645 --> 00:09:07.713
- Yeah. Somebody must have handed you a sniffer and you woke up.

00:09:07.713 --> 00:09:10.950
Listen, the All-Star Game, it's not all about

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:13.920
these fancy goals from the perimeter and dangling.

00:09:14.387 --> 00:09:16.522
It's about getting to the blue paint and scoring the goals

00:09:16.522 --> 00:09:18.824
that matter. Late in games, crunch time, when guys are

00:09:18.824 --> 00:09:22.295
actually buckling down. And I want Joe Pavelski on my team.

00:09:22.295 --> 00:09:24.297
Everybody thought he hit a certain age and he was gonna

00:09:24.297 --> 00:09:27.166
fade off into the sunset and not compete anymore.

00:09:27.166 --> 00:09:33.306
He's already got 20 tucks this year. And it's his fourth All-Star Game.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:34.941
Experience.
- Wow.

00:09:34.941 --> 00:09:38.077
You always need experience in the locker room.

00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:40.079
And he's really good at everything, including golf.

00:09:40.413 --> 00:09:41.280
He's a big hunter.

00:09:42.348 --> 00:09:43.349
Pavs.

00:09:43.349 --> 00:09:45.685
- Biz, I wanna be honest with you right now.

00:09:45.685 --> 00:09:50.323
Your last few picks, you know, I'm looking at my list and

00:09:50.323 --> 00:09:53.092
these guys are maybe not even cracking the top 20 on my list.

00:09:53.092 --> 00:09:56.762
- Oh, that's cute. How many conference finals has Draisaitl and McDavid been to?

00:09:56.762 --> 00:09:58.698
Just off the top of my head. How many?

00:09:59.966 --> 00:10:01.834
- You're right. But listen, Pavelski is the type

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:04.103
of guy, he's scoring the greasy goals in there.
- He's a winner.

00:10:04.103 --> 00:10:06.172
- And are we really getting greasy tips in front in All-Star Games?

00:10:06.172 --> 00:10:08.574
No, we're looking for Michigans.
- Maybe your team won't be.

00:10:08.574 --> 00:10:09.642
- We're looking for Zegras' baseball bats.

00:10:09.642 --> 00:10:12.445
We're looking for, we're looking for some crazy stuff out here, Biz.

00:10:12.445 --> 00:10:15.147
- Maybe your team won't be, but my team will.

00:10:15.147 --> 00:10:16.082
One guy will.

00:10:16.082 --> 00:10:17.183
You need a little bit of everything.

00:10:17.183 --> 00:10:19.619
I mentioned that 200-foot game from Stone coming in.

00:10:19.619 --> 00:10:21.988
Defensive pole checks on the way back.

00:10:21.988 --> 00:10:24.423
You think Ovi's gonna be backchecking like Stone is?

00:10:24.423 --> 00:10:27.426
He'll probably be hungover from bottle service from the night before.
- [Laughing]

00:10:27.426 --> 00:10:31.097
- Stone's gonna be, he's gonna be home by 11 o'clock,
- You're right. You're right. Hey, I can't disagree.

00:10:31.097 --> 00:10:32.632
in bed with the wife and kids.

00:10:33.032 --> 00:10:33.733
And we're good to go.

00:10:33.766 --> 00:10:34.000
- Yup.

